aised as it is (PY7: it became the TypeError)."] [1415 1 "// abstractIsSubclass is abstract_issubclass: c's __bases__ walked, an error other than AttributeError raised"] [1416 1 "// (PY7: it was dropped), the C level's check before each recursion (test_isinstance's"] [1417 1 "// test_infinite_recursion_via_bases_tuple and test_infinite_cycle_in_bases overflowed Go's stack)."] [1452 1 "// posArgs checks a built-in's positional argument count, CPython's messages."] [1470 1 "// ---- object's pickling protocol (typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex__, reduce_newobj, object_getstate) ----"] [1472 1 "// importModule is __import__(name) through the interpreter's builtins (PY5e's import system)."] [1481 1 "// importErrorType is ImportError when the runtime has it, else RuntimeError."] [1497 1 "// objectGetState is object.__getstate__: the instance's __dict__ (None when empty), with its"] [1498 1 "// __slots__' values as a second dictionary."] [1517 3 "// the basic size's check: a built-in base's fields, or slots the names do not cover, cannot be saved"] [1551 1 "// typeSlotNames is _PyType_GetSlotNames: the class's __slotnames__, else copyreg._slotnames's answer; nil for none."] [1612 2 "// reduce_newobj: a state is required of what its arguments, items and pairs do not rebuild"] [1635 1 "// selfMethod puts a built-in method that takes a subclass's instance itself in t's dictionary."] [1641 2 "// object_getstate: object's own __getstate__ with the required check, any other called"] [1650 2 "// set_reduce, deque_reduce, bytearray's _common_reduce: type(self), its items, the state"] [1687 2 "// method_reduce: getattr(self, name)"] [1696 2 "// object___sizeof__: tp_basicsize, here the header's two words"] [1707 3 "// typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex___impl: a __reduce__ overriding object's, a built-in type's too"] [1736 1 "// BuiltinValue is the built-in value an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type carries"] [1737 1 "// (a list subclass's list), else o itself: for t